# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.freeze() suspends all strands under that tag; the strand stays
#         frozen until t2.stop() terminates the outer scope.
# blocked: T39 chk-driver (parallel `,` step) AND v0.10.9-B (user-tag→scope-tag binding) — tag.freeze()/.unfreeze() + SUSPENDED machinery shipped at v0.10.9 W3a+W3c (see tests/chk/tag/freeze_basic.chk for the working minimal fixture)
# matrix-row: tag-freeze
#
# Reason:
#   tag.freeze() requires two M4/M5 features: (1) method dispatch on a UTag
#   value (M4), and (2) the SUSPENDED strand-state machinery that actually
#   halts instruction dispatch for tagged strands (M5).  The ',' separator for
#   concurrent "freeze vs echo" observation also requires the M5 chk driver.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with freeze/unfreeze machinery):
# # var t1 = Tag.new() | {};
# # var t2 = Tag.new() | {};
# # t2: { t1: t1.freeze(); echo("You don't see me") }, sleep(1s);
# # echo("I am the only one");
# # [00000001] *** I am the only one
# # t2.stop();
